# Op2_AllocSubBlock: the two paths no corpus call takes (ruling 5, 2), at its first call.
# pool_empty: the object pool has no free block (g_ObjPoolFree = 0: 140 blocks at scene init,
# every ObjPool_Alloc* takes one), so ObjPool_Alloc fails and the op backs a2 up and yields to
# retry next frame. owned: the handle word a6+offset already holds a block (the op reached again
# on an object that kept its block): no allocation, Op2_ClearNewBlock on that block.

case pool_empty
b $FFFFF4B0 = 0

case owned
w a6 + {a2} = {$FFFFAD52}
